find_objects	CommandSpec { name: "find_objects", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 1, max: 65535, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Find logic hierarchy objects within a scope.", synopsis: ["find_objects scope -pattern search_pattern ?-object_type model|inst|port|supply_port|net|process? ?-direction in|out|inout? ?-transitive ?TRUE|FALSE?? ?-regexp? ?-exact? ?-ignore_case? ?-non_leaf? ?-leaf_only? ?-traverse_macros? ?-expand_to_bits?"], snippet: "Searches the logic hierarchy under a given scope for instances, nets, ports, supply ports, or processes whose name matches a pattern -- a Tcl glob expression by default, or a regular expression with -regexp, or a literal with -exact -- optionally restricted by object type, port or supply-port direction, leaf or non-leaf status, and transitivity through the descendant subtree, which stops at leaf cells and macros unless -traverse_macros is given. The -expand_to_bits option additionally expands multi-bit port and net matches down to individual bit names. The search is restricted to the specified scope, which shall be the current scope or reside in or below it. The command is a query only and is not itself saved into output UPF, though its results can be embedded there by other commands.", source: "IEEE 1801-2024 §6.33", examples: "find_objects A/B/D -pattern *BW1*  -object_type inst  -transitive TRUE", return_value: "A list of names, relative to the current scope, of the objects that match the search criteria, carrying just the object names without any indication of object type and possibly mixing more than one type, or the empty string when nothing matches." }), forms: [FormSpec { kind: Default, synopsis: "find_objects scope -pattern search_pattern ?-object_type model|inst|port|supply_port|net|process? ?-direction in|out|inout? ?-transitive ?TRUE|FALSE?? ?-regexp? ?-exact? ?-ignore_case? ?-non_leaf? ?-leaf_only? ?-traverse_macros? ?-expand_to_bits?", surface: None, lifecycle: Lifecycle { introduced: None, deprecated: None, retired: None, deprecation_fix: None } }], command_forms: [], semantic_operation: None, semantic_operation_windows: [], completion: None, result_stability: None, native_result: None, assigns_variable_at: None, safe_on_uninit: None, const_fold: None, const_fold_versioned: None, lowering_hook: None, bpf_op: None, codegen_hook: None, codegen_hook_windows: [], inline_codegen_hook: None, inline_codegen_hook_windows: [], native_lowering: None, native_lowering_windows: [], semantics: Inherited, analyser_hook: None, command_table_effect: None, side_effects: [], world_effects: None, state_transitions: None, dispatch_dependencies: None, literal_argument_validator: None, source_index_bounds: None, inferred_storage_type: None, required_package: Some("upf"), tk_geometry: None, excluded_events: [], unsafe_command: false, closed_value_args: [], arg_values_accept_prefix: false, event_requires: None, event_requirement_forms: [], event_emits: None, event_emission_forms: [], data_collection: None, irules_source_flow: None, side_switch_target: None, event_handler_priority: None, irules_top_leve