map_power_switch	CommandSpec { name: "map_power_switch", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 1, max: 65535, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Specify which power-switch model is to be used for the implementation of the corresponding switch instance.", synopsis: ["map_power_switch switch_name_list -lib_cells lib_cell_list ?-port_map {{mapped_model_port switch_port_or_supply_net_ref}...}?"], snippet: "Explicitly specifies which power-switch library-cell model implements a given create_power_switch instance, and optionally maps model ports to switch ports or supply-net references rather than relying on automatic name-based association. When -port_map is omitted, ports of the switch instance are associated to library-cell ports by name matching, and it is then an error for any port on either side to remain unmapped. Manual mapping may cause the implementation to diverge from the RTL specification, which can defeat logical-equivalence checking.", source: "IEEE 1801-2024 §6.37", examples: "map_power_switch switch_sw1  -lib_cells {sw1}  -port_map {\n                {inp1   vin1}\n  