map_retention_clamp_cell	CommandSpec { name: "map_retention_clamp_cell", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 1, max: 65535, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Specify a list of library cells used for implementation of clamp cells for clock and async paths of retention strategies.", synopsis: ["map_retention_clamp_cell list_of_strategies -domain domain_name -clock_clamp_lib_cells list_of_clock_path_library_cells -async_clamp_lib_cells list_of_async_path_library_cells"], snippet: "Specifies, for one or more retention strategies on a domain, which library cells may be used to implement the clamp cells inserted on the clock path and on the async set/reset path of the resulting retention cells; only isolation or enable level-shifter library cells are allowed in either list. It shall be an error if domain_name is not found, or if none of the strategies listed in list_of_strategies are defined on domain_name.", source: "IEEE 1801-2024 §6.40", examples: "set_retention RET1 -domain PD1 ...\nmap_retention_cell RET1 -domain PD1 -lib_cells {zpr_LC1}\nmap_retention_clamp_cell {RET1} -domai