set_correlated	CommandSpec { name: "set_correlated", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 0, max: 65535, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Declare that supply nets' or sets' voltage variation ranges are to be treated as correlated when being compared.", synopsis: ["set_correlated ?-nets {supply_net_name_list...}? ?-sets {supply_set_name_list...}?"], snippet: "Declares that two or more supply ports, supply nets, or supply-set power and ground functions have correlated voltage-variation ranges, so that minimum is compared to minimum and maximum to maximum -- naming ports, nets, or supply-set functions directly with -nets, or naming supply sets with -sets so that their power and ground functions are correlated together. One or the other of these options, but not both, shall be specified. Supplies declared equivalent are always deemed correlated, but using set_correlated does not make supplies equivalent.", source: "IEEE 1801-2024 §6.43", examples: "set_correlated -nets {{VDD1 VDD2}}\nset_correlated -sets {{SS1 SS2}}", return_value: "The empty string if successful; otherwise a TCL