sim_assertion_control	CommandSpec { name: "sim_assertion_control", pack_source_sandbox_helper: false, traits: Traits(0), surface: Some([SpecSurface { provider: Core(Tcl), windows: [("8.4", Some("9.2"))] }]), arity: Arity { count: Arguments, min: 0, max: 65535, step: 0, also_exact: None }, arity_windows: [], arg_roles: [], arg_role_resolver: None, arg_role_count_resolver: None, arg_role_layout_resolver: None, arg_role_resolver_roles: [], clause_grammar: None, arg_presentation: [], repeated_args: [], frame_effect: None, clause_shape_check: None, command_prefixes: [], command_prefix_resolver: None, script_timing_resolver: None, script_lookup_scope: None, substitution_resolver: None, callback_taint_inputs: [], return_type: None, return_type_hook: None, var_write_typing: ReturnValue, variable_write_min_args: None, return_elements: None, var_elements_effect: None, representation_effect: None, arg_types: [], subcommands: [], prefix_matching: Enabled, allow_unknown_subcommands: false, default_form_first_word: None, hover: Some(HoverSnippet { summary: "Control the behavior of assertions during low-power verification.", synopsis: ["sim_assertion_control ?-elements element_list? ?-exclude_elements exclude_list? ?-domain domain_name? ?-model model_name? ?-controlling_domain domain_name? ?-control_expr boolean_expression? ?-type reset|suspend|kill? ?-transitive ?TRUE|FALSE??"], snippet: "Disables, resets, or suspends assertions during low-power verification so that non-power-aware assertions can be used correctly in a power-aware environment. -type selects suspend, reset, or kill behavior, and -control_expr or -controlling_domain, or by default the domain containing the assertion, determine when the control is active based on whether the relevant primary supply is NORMAL. It shall be an error if both -controlling_domain and -control_expr are specified in the same command.", source: "IEEE 1801-2024 §6.58", examples: "sim_assertion_control -elements L1/clock_not_x -type kill\nsim_